hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17909","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hasanah, he said, We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and we camped in a land with many lizards. So we caught some and slaughtered them. While the pots were boiling with them, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said, A nation from the Children of Israel was lost, and I fear these may be they, so overturn them. So we overturned them."
"17910","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hasanah, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with something like a shield in his hand. So he put it down then sat, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinated toward it. Some of the people said, Look at him urinating as a woman urinates. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard him and said, Woe to you, do you not know what befell the man of the Children of Israel. When anything of urine touched them they would cut it off with scissors, then he forbade them, so he was punished in his grave."
"17911","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Amash, and Waki narrated to us, he said, al-Amash narrated to me with the same meaning, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hasanah, Waki said, al-Juhani, he said, We raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and famine struck us. We camped in a land with many lizards, so we took some and cooked them in our pots. We asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said, A nation was lost, or was transformed, Yahya doubted, and Allah knows best. So he ordered us and we overturned the pots. Waki said, was transformed, so I fear these may be they, so we overturned them though we were hungry."
"17912","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hasanah, he said, I and Amr ibn al-As were sitting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with a shield or something like it, screened himself with it, and urinated sitting. So we said, Does the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinate as a woman urinates. Then he came to us and said, Do you not know what befell the man of the Children of Israel. When anything of urine touched a man among them he would cut it off, then he forbade them that, so he was punished in his grave."
